# The map's tile provider, read at build time. The repository names none: give all four or the
# map has a plain background and asks no tile server for anything. Only the provider's host is
# allowed to receive a request, and only for tiles. Read the provider's terms before a public link.
#
# Example, with a synthetic host:
#   VITE_TILE_URL_TEMPLATE=https://tiles.provider.test/base/{z}/{x}/{y}.png
#   VITE_TILE_ATTRIBUTION=Map data by the Provider, CC BY
#   VITE_TILE_SOURCE_NAME=Provider Maps
#   VITE_TILE_TERMS_URL=https://provider.test/terms
#
# One or more templates, separated by white space, each with {z}, {x} and {y}:
VITE_TILE_URL_TEMPLATE=
# The attribution the provider requires:
VITE_TILE_ATTRIBUTION=
# The provider's name, shown with its terms under the map:
VITE_TILE_SOURCE_NAME=
# The address of the provider's terms of use, shown as text:
VITE_TILE_TERMS_URL=
